{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":814,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Ps.77","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Psalms","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Psalms 77","reference":"Psalms 77","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"The psalmist complains of deep distress, and temptations to despair, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"1-10.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"He encourages himself to hope, by the remembrance of what God had done formerly, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":4,"text":"11-20.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":5,"text":"To the chief musician, to Jeduthun, A psalm of Asaph.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":6,"text":"2.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":7,"text":"Night - Which to others was a time of rest and quietness.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":8,"text":"3.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":9,"text":"Troubled - Yea, the thoughts of God were now a matter of trouble, because he was angry with me.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":10,"text":"Overwhelmed - So far was I from finding relief.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":11,"text":"4.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":12,"text":"Waking - By continual grief.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":13,"text":"5.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":14,"text":"The days - The mighty works of God in former times.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":15,"text":"6.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":16,"text":"My song - The mercies of God vouchsafed to me, and to his people, which have obliged me to sing his praises, not only in the day, but also by night.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":17,"text":"7.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":18,"text":"Cut off - His peculiar people.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":19,"text":"10.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":20,"text":"I said - These suspicions of God's faithfulness proceed from the weakness of my faith.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":21,"text":"The years - The years wherein God hath done great and glorious works, which are often ascribed to God's right-hand.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":22,"text":"13.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":23,"text":"In holiness - God is holy and just, and true in all his works.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":24,"text":"16.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":25,"text":"Afraid - And stood still, as men astonished, do.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":26,"text":"17.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":27,"text":"Poured - When the Israelites passed over the sea.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":28,"text":"Arrows - Hail-stones or lightnings.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":29,"text":"19.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":19,"scriptureVerseEnd":19},{"verse":30,"text":"Not known - Because the water returned and covered them.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":19,"scriptureVerseEnd":19},{"verse":31,"text":"20.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":20,"scriptureVerseEnd":20},{"verse":32,"text":"Leddest - First through the sea, and afterwards through the wilderness, with singular care and tenderness, as a shepherd doth his sheep.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":20,"scriptureVerseEnd":20}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Psalms","chapter":77}}